    section: "C", questionRef: "2015 HL Section C Q2(c)(ii)",
    stem: "Loudspeakers are used in many multimedia devices.",
    questionText: "Describe, using notes and annotated sketches, the operation of a loudspeaker or a microphone.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal","notation":"(14 marks,8+6)"}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "At the front of a loudspeaker, there is a fabric, plastic, paper, or lightweight metal cone (diaphragm-4 ). The outer part of the cone is fastened to the outer part of the loudspeaker's circular metal rim.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "The inner part is fixed to an iron coil (voice coil-2) that sits just in front of a permanent magnet (1).", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "When you connect the loudspeaker to a stereo, electrical signals feed through the speaker cables into the coil. This turns the coil into a temporary magnet or electromagnet. As the electricity flows back and forth in the cables, the electromagnet either attracts or repels the permanent magnet. This moves the coil back and forward, pulling and pushing the loudspeaker cone. Sound is created.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "The process is reversed for a microphone.", marks: null, openList: true },
    ],
