    stem: "‘Capacity planning’ is a way to analyse demand for a product and find an economical means of meeting that demand.",
    questionText: "Capacity can be managed using the following strategies: • Capacity lead strategy • Capacity lag strategy • Average capacity strategy. Distinguish clearly, with specific examples, between these capacity strategies.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal","notation":"(14 marks, 8+6)"}, totalMarks: 8,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Capacity lead strategy always sufficient capacity to meet demand and any growth, improving in- frastructure (shops) in anticipation of potential new customers from competitors, etc.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "Capacity lag strategy adding capacity after demand growth, e.g., order placed for new cars.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "Average capacity strategy trying to maintain capacity and meet short-term surges in demand, toys for sale in shops at Christmas, etc.", marks: null, openList: true },
    ],
